MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Twenty-five files that no route, component, hook or lib imports. Found by
walking reachability from every file under app/ (plus middleware), following
static imports, dynamic import() and require(), resolving both @/ and
relative specifiers: 56 component files are reachable, these were not.

Every name was then grepped by hand. The only hits outside their own files
are three comments, which are the story:

  page.tsx:17        "NotificationsBell removed from topbar 2026-05-17 —
                      the inbox is now an ordinary sidebar view."
  WorkflowSidebar    "My Tasks retired Aug 2026: it was All Tasks with one
                      filter applied, and two lists of the same rows meant
                      two places to look."
  AQWatermark.tsx:6  "It draws itself in exactly the way AnimatedAQLogo
                      does — the A's centreline…"

Each was replaced, the replacement said why, and the original stayed on disk.

Four of them share a filename with a live screen — ClientsView,
ContractsView, VendorsView, DashboardView — in components/clients/,
components/contracts/, components/vendors/ and components/dashboard/, which
look exactly like where the real ones would live. The live ones are all in
components/workflow/. Opening the wrong one and editing it for an hour is a
matter of time; it has already happened.

Kept, because something live still uses them:

  components/ui/Avatar.tsx   MyProfileCard imports it
  lib/utils.ts               Avatar imports getInitials
  types/index.ts             Avatar and lib/utils import types from it

hooks/use-supabase.ts is 790 lines imported by nothing; use-workflow.ts is
the one in use, by 38 files.

